auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{apiKey}}
}

docs {
  Postman Email API (`/v1`). Requests authenticate with either:

  - **API key**: set the `apiKey` secret in your environment (Bruno keeps secret values out of the `.bru` files). Sent as `Authorization: Bearer <apiKey>`.
  - **Cookie session**: run `Auth/Request OTP`, then `Auth/Verify OTP and log in`. Bruno stores the session cookie. Some routes (API keys, settings, attachments) only accept the cookie.

  The backend checks the cookie before the API key. Once you're logged in, API-key requests run as the logged-in user, so log out (or clear Bruno's cookies) before testing an API key.

  Never commit real API keys, OTPs, recipient addresses or campaign data.
}
